Unlock with Front Camera is a new option in iOS 27.3. If you turn it on, you can quickly unlock the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; when it's closed.<br/>
<br/>
It's a feature that only works at the Lock Screen when the Duo is closed, so you can't use it for authenticating <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-pay/">Apple Pay</a> purchases or inserting logins and passwords from the Passwords app. You also need to use <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> or a passcode for unlocking the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; when it's unfolded.<br/>
<br/>
Face unlock can be turned on in the &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj; &amp; Passcode section of the Settings app, and it works fairly well when it's active. You aren't going to have much luck in a dark room because it's just using the standard front camera, but if the lighting is decent, you can unlock without &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also added a "Close to Lock" feature that locks the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; when you close it instead of transferring content to the outer display.<br/>
<br/>
